s; the author's own answer is that the Fiends have no loyalty to Caesar. A faint Legion stain over somebody else's ground is precisely that argument.","claimSource":"docs/changes/map-timeline/lore-contention-2026-08-14.md","geomSource":"geography/kml/factions.geojson#factions-fiends-territory-3b33123f","precedence":2},"geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[-115.183471,36.090568],[-115.193957,36.097799],[-115.21284,36.101683],[-115.242365,36.103347],[-115.251975,36.120613],[-115.251288,36.132053],[-115.247342,36.142475],[-115.238417,36.153589],[-115.239445,36.163481],[-115.249915,36.171349],[-115.263193,36.176255],[-115.290688,36.174501],[-115.31103,36.162547],[-115.332744,36.148821],[-115.327977,36.125461],[-115.301245,36.114022],[-115.289401,36.083372],[-115.285624,36.051458],[-115.272578,36.029527],[-115.242805,36.007729],[-115.197144,36.00023],[-115.120143,36.005645],[-115.090617,36.01231],[-115.081347,36.021197],[-115.079974,36.033136],[-115.087784,36.037786],[-115.105465,36.041603],[-115.134734,36.047155],[-115.159625,36.051874],[-115.175589,36.055482],[-115.176447,36.064815],[-115.177735,36.073106],[-115.183471,36.090568]]]}}],"_consumers":{"wendover-corridors":"tools/build-influence-corridors.py","contested-holdings":"tools/build-influence-claims.py"},"_contestedPoints":{"1":"drawn - NCR presence at San Francisco and an NCR field over the Shi","2":"drawn - NCR presence at Junktown and Bakersfield","3":"drawn - Legion presence at Yuma","4":"drawn - Legion presence at Nipton","5":"drawn - Legion field over Fiends Territory and a Legion presence at Camp McCarran","6":"drawn - NCR presence at Novac","7":"drawn - NCR presence at Vault City and at New Reno","8":"NOT A FEATURE. 'Exact borders are anachronistic for a polity of a few hundred thousand' is the methodological criticism the channel answers by existing; there is no place to put a mark.","9":"ALREADY DRAWN, in the era channel. savannah-2313-influence-2313.geojson carries the six trading spheres with channel=influence. It is dated 2313 and the present day is 2296, so it cannot become a present-day claim until the channel takes date ranges.","10":"ALREADY DRAWN, in the era channel, as the same 2313 layer's Dissident belt. Same date obstacle as point 9.","11":"CANNOT YET. The 2290 sheet's lighter fills are author-confirmed influence, but the extraction reads that sheet's fills as one class. The technique exists - westcoast-2281-names.py measures a polygon's dominant fill and writes channelSuspect - and has never been run against the 2290 sheet.","12":"ALREADY DRAWN, in the era channel. ncr-2253-control-2253.geojson carries channel=deJure on 4 features and channel=deFacto on 28, which is the author's own intent. Dated 2253.","13":"CANNOT YET. The Deep South sheet's legend footnote denies that its borders imply governance, but no geometry from that sheet is extracted, so there is nothing to stain."}}
